# Locator Strategy (eFMS / eTMS)

Full reference: `ruleAi.md` Sections 3.4, 3.9.

## Priority (semantic first — not styling)

1. `aria-label`, `role`, Playwright `getByRole` / `getByLabel` when they resolve
2. `data-testid`, `data-qa`, `data-test`
3. Stable `id`, `name`, `formcontrolname`
4. Visible text (`:has-text`, `normalize-space()`)
5. Scoped CSS
6. Relative XPath anchored to `href`, `h3`, `th`, form container
7. `contains(@class, ...)` — fallback only

## FORBIDDEN

- Dynamic/hashed classes, random auto-generated ids
- Absolute positional XPath (`/html/body/...`, `//div[3]/button[2]`)
- `nth` / index as primary selector
- Broad selectors (`input[type='text']`, bare `button`) except documented last resort

## Before commit — verify on live DOM

1. Exactly one match in scope
2. User-interactable element (not overlay/spinner)
3. Survives reload / re-navigation
4. Stable: loading → loaded → with data

## Rules

- All locators in Page Object `*_selectors: list[str]` — best first
- Never `page.locator()` in tests — use `pages` fixture
- Never guess — inspect UAT at 1920×1080 headed first
